 falls in her current Assembly term.\n- **What the bill does:** Section 220.5 bars schools from enacting or enforcing any policy that would require staff to disclose a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent.\n- **Why not rung 1:** Section 220.3 only says staff \"shall not be required\" to disclose. It does not require staff to keep the information from parents.\n- **Two judgement calls:**\n  - I treated the bill as single-subject: its other parts (resources for parents and a ban on retaliating against staff) all concern the same pupil-rights subject.\n  - I read a state law that forbids local disclosure rules as on-question, not as preemption, because rung 2 is itself about forbidding such rules.\n- **Rests on:** both passages, the vote page and the bill text.\n- **Left empty:** `needs_source` and `quotes`. The sources contain none of her own words.\n\nThe GitHub plugin failed to connect, and several claude.ai connectors (Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey, WorkOS) need authorising in their connector settings. This task used none of them.","ttft_ms":10503,"type":"result","duration_ms":27391,"uuid":"26e6d402-1711-443d-8289-31129b5ab684","ttft_stream_ms":1356,"time_to_request_ms":99,"first_content_frame_ms":1356,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
